<title>CHILE: Codelco Andina 1996 copper output rises 6 pct.</title>
<headline>Codelco Andina 1996 copper output rises 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andina, the third largest of Chilean state copper company Codelco's four mines, produced 154,421 tonnes of copper last year, up from 145,793 tonnes in 1995, an official at the division told Reuters.</p>
<p>Andina's molybdenum output rose to 2,002 tonnes in 1996 from 1,656 tonnes in 1995, he said.</p>
<p>The division is carrying out a previously announced major expansion plan which will increase output to 220,000 tonnes of copper in concentrates by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((--Rodrigo Martinez, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
